   a. Weed Management: Control weeds, especially those that can serve as hosts for the SB. This helps reduce the overall population of the fungus and the SB population.

   b. Weed-free crops: Avoid planting any crops that can attract the SB near the coffee crop.

   c. Proper Harvesting: Remove and destroy dead or dead-aged plants and dead leaves, as these can be hosts for the SB.

   d. Proper Irrigation: Ensure proper irrigation to prevent stress on the plants, as stressed plants are more susceptible to SB infections.

