The effect is as follows:

1. Increased Blood Pressure → Increased Baroreceptor Activity: When blood pressure increases, the arterial baroreceptors (located in the carotid sinus and the femoral sinus) become more stretched and thus become more active. They release more norepinephrine (adrenergic) and serotonin (paraminergic) into the parasympathetic nervous system.

2. Transmission to the NTS: The norepinephrine and serotonin are transmitted to the NTS via the parasympathetic nervous system.

