","To find the maximum height reached by the particle, we use the kinematic equations for motion under constant acceleration. The initial velocity is \( v_0 = 20 \, \text{m/s} \), the acceleration is \( a = -9.8 \, \text{m/s}^2 \) (downward), and the final velocity at the maximum height is \( v = 0 \, \text{m/s} \). The final height is \( h \), which we want to find.

