2. Pressure: The pressure during synthesis can also influence the zeolite's structure and properties. High pressure can lead to the formation of more stable structures, while low pressure can result in more porous structures.

3. pH: The pH of the solution can affect the solubility of the reactants and the formation of zeolite nuclei. By controlling the pH, it is possible to control the size and shape of the zeolite particles.

