3. Reactor Residence Time (RRT): The RRTT is the average time a material is in the reactor. It is inversely proportional to the reactor space velocity. A longer RRTT can lead to a higher conversion of reactants to surfactants, but it can also result in increased side reactions and degradation of the surfactant. The optimal RRTT is a trade-off between these factors.

