The complex `[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]Cl2` dissociates in an aqueous solution as follows:
\[
[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]Cl2 \rightarrow [Pt(NH3)4Cl2]^{2+} + 2Cl^-
\]
Thus, the complex `[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]Cl2` dissociates into `[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]^{2+}` and two chloride ions. 

Thus, the number of chloride ions produced is 2. 

Final Answer: \(\boxed{2}\)
