- \(g_n\) is the normal gravity
- \(G\) is the gravitational constant (\(6.6740357 \times 10^{-11} \, \text{N m}^2/\text{kg}^2\))
- \(M\) is the Earth's mass (\(5.9761 \times 10^{24} \, \text{kg}\))
- \(a\) is the Earth's equatorial radius (km)
- \(R\) is the Earth's mean radius (km)
- \(r\) is the distance to the center of the Earth (km)

The first-order approximation simplifies the formula to:

\[
g_n = \frac{GM}{a^2}
\]

