","Plasma-based astrophysical phenomena, such as solar flares and coronal mass ejections (CMEs), are fundamentally different from other astrophysical phenomena due to their unique physical properties. These properties are primarily due to the high temperatures and densities that lead to the formation of plasma, a state of matter where electrons are stripped from atoms, leaving a collection of charged particles. These properties affect the behavior of the plasma in these phenomena in several ways, leading to the unique phenomena we observe.

